    text:"Oxford University launched the British Open-ended Learning & Discovery Lab (BOLD), a fully-funded research initiative recruiting 'BOLD Fellows'—researchers with high agency and 3 million GPU-hours in initial allocation, targeting roughly 5,000 H100-equivalent compute. The lab emphasizes open-ended discovery rather than predefined milestones and operates independently from UK government AI policy, though funded through government research grants. Jakob Foerster (MIT/OpenAI affiliations) leads recruitment.",
