    text:"SoftBank Group announced a record ¥1 trillion ($6.3 billion) retail bond sale, the largest ever by any Japanese company, with 7-year bonds priced Aug 24 at a coupon range of 4.3% to 4.9%. The proceeds will fund AI initiatives and debt repayment, including support for OpenAI projects. This is SoftBank's third retail bond issuance this year, following ¥418 billion in April and ¥260 billion in June, signaling rapid capital mobilization to support its expanding AI investment commitments.",
    why:"A Japanese industrial giant raising a record $6.3B via retail bonds specifically to fund OpenAI investments reveals how geopolitically distributed capital is now flowing into AI-infrastructure support on the same scale as venture funding—distinct from tech-company cash and representing state-adjacent capital committing to frontier AI at scale.",
