    source:{ name:"Nvidia", handle:"Nvidia", platform:"web", kind:"lab" },
    text:"Nvidia announced that Groq 3 LPX, its dedicated low-latency inference accelerator acquired through the $20 billion Groq acquisition last December, has entered full production and will come online before the end of 2026. Nebius will be the first AI cloud to deploy it through the Nebius Token Factory platform. Each liquid-cooled LPX rack houses 256 language processing units alongside Vera Rubin GPUs, delivering up to 35x more inference throughput per megawatt of power compared to GPU-only systems, targeting 3,400 tokens per second.",
    why:"A completed hardware acquisition integration shipping into production ahead of end-of-year—with a concrete first customer already deployed—signals Nvidia's successful consolidation of a specialized inference accelerator and Nebius's commitment to inference-optimized infrastructure, distinct from training systems and representing a major shift in how data-center topology now segregates compute by workload type.",
